# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from using the server-side Sampler and Estimator to the client-side implementations of these primitives in IBM Quantum Compute Service"
msgstr "Esegui la migrazione dall'uso di Sampler ed Estimator lato server alle implementazioni lato client di queste primitive in IBM Quantum Compute Service"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator"
msgstr "Migra da Sampler ed Estimator lato server a lato client"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator {#migrate-from-server-side-to-client-side-sampler-and-estimator}"
msgstr "Migra da Sampler ed Estimator lato server a lato client {#migrate-from-server-side-to-client-side-sampler-and-estimator}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This guide describes how to migrate from the **server-side** implementations of IBM Quantum&reg;\n"
"`Sampler` and `Estimator` to their new **client-side** implementations in\n"
"`qiskit-ibm-runtime`. The interfaces and options are largely unchanged, so most code\n"
"runs as-is, but there are some behavioral differences to understand.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questa guida descrive come eseguire la migrazione dalle implementazioni **lato server** di IBM Quantum&reg;\n"
"`Sampler` ed `Estimator` alle loro nuove implementazioni **lato client** in\n"
"`qiskit-ibm-runtime`. Le interfacce e le opzioni sono in gran parte invariate, quindi la maggior parte del codice\n"
"viene eseguita così com'è, ma ci sono alcune differenze di comportamento da comprendere.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Contesto {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Sampler and Estimator are primitive *interfaces* defined in Qiskit. The IBM Quantum\n"
"Compute Service (formerly Qiskit Runtime) has historically provided the *implementation*\n"
"of these primitives inside its runtime environment. When you call `sampler.run()` or\n"
"`estimator.run()`, the request is sent to the service, and **all** computation — including\n"
"error suppression and mitigation — happens on the server side.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sampler ed Estimator sono *interfacce* primitive definite in Qiskit. IBM Quantum\n"
"Compute Service (precedentemente Qiskit Runtime) ha storicamente fornito l'*implementazione*\n"
"di queste primitive all'interno del proprio ambiente runtime. Quando chiami `sampler.run()` o\n"
"`estimator.run()`, la richiesta viene inviata al servizio e **tutto** il calcolo — inclusi\n"
"la soppressione e la mitigazione degli errori — avviene lato server.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This black-box experience is convenient: you don't have to worry about implementation\n"
"details. But it also makes the primitives hard to debug, customize, or learn from,\n"
"because you can't see what happens during processing.\n"
msgstr ""
"Questa esperienza black-box è conveniente: non devi preoccuparti dei dettagli\n"
"implementativi. Ma rende anche le primitive difficili da debuggare, personalizzare o da cui imparare,\n"
"perché non puoi vedere cosa succede durante l'elaborazione.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The newly introduced [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model#directed-execution-model-beta) takes the opposite approach and\n"
"provides a **white-box** experience. All design intents are captured on the client side,\n"
"and a single server-side primitive [**Executor**](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive) processes those inputs exactly as\n"
"directed — it makes no implicit decisions on your behalf.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il [modello di esecuzione diretta](/guides/directed-execution-model#directed-execution-model-beta) introdotto di recente adotta l'approccio opposto e\n"
"fornisce un'esperienza **white-box**. Tutte le intenzioni progettuali vengono catturate lato client,\n"
"e un'unica primitiva lato server [**Executor**](/guides/directed-execution-model#executor-primitive) elabora tali input esattamente come\n"
"indicato — non prende decisioni implicite per tuo conto.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, Sampler and Estimator are re-implemented\n"
"on the **client side** on top of Executor. They provide the same convenience and\n"
"abstraction as before, and now you can inspect the implementation details when you need\n"
"to. Because the interfaces and options remain largely the same, migration should be\n"
"seamless.\n"
msgstr ""
"A partire da `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, Sampler ed Estimator vengono reimplementati\n"
"lato **client** sopra Executor. Offrono la stessa comodità e\n"
"astrazione di prima, e ora puoi ispezionare i dettagli implementativi quando ne hai\n"
"bisogno. Poiché le interfacce e le opzioni rimangono in gran parte le stesse, la migrazione dovrebbe essere\n"
"senza soluzione di continuità.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note: IBM Quantum only supports version 2 of Sampler and Estimator interfaces (`BaseSamplerV2` and `BaseEstimatorV2`). Therefore, they are simply referred to as Sampler and Estimator in this guide.\n"
msgstr "Nota: IBM Quantum supporta solo la versione 2 delle interfacce Sampler ed Estimator (`BaseSamplerV2` e `BaseEstimatorV2`). Pertanto, in questa guida vengono semplicemente indicati come Sampler ed Estimator.\n"

